      "Synthetic guide to alpha hydroxy acids",
      "What alpha hydroxy acids are"
    ],
    "ordinal": 0,
    "text": "In this synthetic guide, alpha hydroxy acids (AHAs) are a family of acids used in some cosmetic products. Glycolic acid and lactic acid are the examples this guide names. The guide describes them as exfoliating ingredients found in some cleansers, toners, and creams.",
