    "section_path": [
      "Synthetic guide to retinoids and retinol",
      "Irritation caution"
    ],
    "ordinal": 0,
    "text": "The synthetic guide warns that retinoids and retinol can cause irritation, including dryness, peeling, and redness, especially when someone first starts using them. However, the guide says this irritation often lessens as skin adjusts, and it advises stopping and asking a dermatologist if irritation is severe.",
    "start_char": 564,
    "end_char": 875,
    "content_hash": "sha256:848e5cd0b4c4742c2a33225019d58da15a9cfdadf4aec208b4845f2abf257882",
